<div class="abc-info">
  <h4 class="card-title mb-3">What is ABC Analysis?</h4>
  <p class="fs-6 text-muted">ABC Analysis helps you categorize menu items based on <strong>sales volume and profitability</strong>, allowing you to focus on what truly drives revenue.</p>

  <ul class="list-unstyled d-grid gap-2 mb-4">
    <li class="d-flex align-items-start">
      <span class="badge bg-success-subtle text-success me-2 mt-1 rounded-circle p-1">
        <i class="ti ti-a-b-c fs-4"></i>
      </span>
      <div>
        <strong>A-Category</strong> – Top-performing items (usually 70-80% of revenue). Focus on <strong>maintaining quality, consistency, and strategic pricing</strong>.
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="d-flex align-items-start">
      <span class="badge bg-info-subtle text-info me-2 mt-1 rounded-circle p-1">
        <i class="ti ti-a-b-c fs-4"></i>
      </span>
      <div>
        <strong>B-Category</strong> – Supporting items (usually 15-20% of revenue). Optimize pricing, marketing, and <strong>positioning</strong> to move them into the 'A' category.
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="d-flex align-items-start">
      <span class="badge bg-warning-subtle text-warning me-2 mt-1 rounded-circle p-1">
        <i class="ti ti-a-b-c fs-4"></i>
      </span>
      <div>
        <strong>C-Category</strong> – Least impactful items (usually 5-10% of revenue). Consider <strong>improving, repositioning, or removing</strong> them to free up resources.
      </div>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p class="fw-semibold">Use ABC Analysis to optimize menu pricing, reduce waste, and maximize profitability.</p>
</div>